Notebook[{Cell["Representative MagneticTB Models", "Title"], Cell["This page collects models that require more than the two-band graphene example. They include unequal orbital dimensions on two atoms, several Wyckoff orbits, spinful magnetic symmetry, induced representations, and an antiunitary operation that carries a state from one site to another. Each section gives the complete input and then shows the resulting Hamiltonian, orbital order or hopping, symmetry matrices, and bands.", "Text"], Cell["Load MagneticTB", "Section"], Cell[BoxData["Needs[\"MagneticTB`\"]"], "Input"], Cell["SimpleCubicS: one s orbital on a simple-cubic site", "Section"], Cell["Place one s orbital at the origin of a simple-cubic lattice. The gray Pm-3m group keeps this site fixed, and the six bonds in shell 2 connect it to the nearest cells along plus or minus x, y, and z. The resulting one-band Hamiltonian contains one onsite energy and the usual sum of three cosine dispersions.", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["simpleCubicOperations = msgop[gray[221]];\ninit[\n  lattice -> {\n    {a, 0, 0},\n    {0, a, 0},\n    {0, 0, a}\n  },\n  lattpar -> {a -> 1},\n  wyckoffposition -> {\n    {{0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}\n  },\n  symminformation -> simpleCubicOperations,\n  basisFunctions -> {{\"s\"}},\n  InitialBondShells -> 2,\n  GenerateSymmetryGroup -> False\n];\nsimpleCubicHamiltonian = Sum[symham[i], {i, 2}];\nvalidationBandPath = {\n  {{{0, 0, 0}, {1/2, 0, 0}}, {\"G\", \"X\"}},\n  {{{1/2, 0, 0}, {1/2, 1/2, 0}}, {\"X\", \"M\"}},\n  {{{1/2, 1/2, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}, {\"M\", \"G\"}}\n};"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData["orbitalTable[]"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{TemplateBox[{"\"Hamiltonian dimension = \"", "1", "\"; representation mode = \"", "\"DirectProduct\""}, "RowDefault"], "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""}, {"\"H index\"", "\"Site\"", "\"Wyckoff orbit\"", "\"Atom\"", "\"Fractional position\"", "\"Cartesian position\"", "\"Local orbital\"", "\"Input basis\"", "\"Actual basis state\"", "\"Spin structure\"", "\"Spin state\"", "\"Transport operation\""}, {"1", "1", "1", "1", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "1", "\"s\"", "1", "\"Spinless\"", "None", "None"}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, GridBoxFrame -> {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}], "Grid"]], "Output"], Cell[BoxData["MatrixForm[simpleCubicHamiltonian]"], "Input"], Cell[BoxData[TagBox[RowBox[{"(", "⁠", GridBox[{{RowBox[{"e1", "+", RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", ""}], " ", "kx"}]], " ", "t1"}], "+", RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["", RowBox[{"", " ", "kx"}]], " ", "t1"}], "+", RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", ""}], " ", "ky"}]], " ", "t1"}], "+", RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["", RowBox[{"", " ", "ky"}]], " ", "t1"}], "+", RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", ""}], " ", "kz"}]], " ", "t1"}], "+", RowBox[{SuperscriptBox["", RowBox[{"", " ", "kz"}]], " ", "t1"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnSpacings -> 1, RowAlignments -> Baseline, ColumnAlignments -> Center], "⁠", ")"}], Function[BoxForm`e$, MatrixForm[BoxForm`e$]]]], "Output"], Cell[BoxData["bandManipulate[validationBandPath, 30, simpleCubicHamiltonian]"], "Input"], Cell["CsCl: a 1 by 3 rectangular s-p hopping block", "Section"], Cell["The corner site carries one s orbital and the body-centred site carries px, py, pz. The off-diagonal row below is therefore the actual rectangular hopping block; it is not required to be a square or Hermitian matrix by itself.", "Text"], Cell[BoxData["csclOperations = msgop[gray[221]];\ninit[\n  lattice -> {\n    {a, 0, 0},\n    {0, a, 0},\n    {0, 0, a}\n  },\n  lattpar -> {a -> 1},\n  wyckoffposition -> {\n    {{0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}},\n    {{1/2, 1/2, 1/2}, {0, 0, 0}}\n  },\n  symminformation -> csclOperations,\n  basisFunctions -> {{\"s\"}, {\"px\", \"py\", \"pz\"}},\n  Initia